## Reference override (read first)

When the user provides **reference screenshots**, an **existing web module**, or asks to **match / clone / exact parity**:

- **Parity beats creativity.** Match the reference layout, copy, hierarchy, and visual details first.
- Do not redesign toward generic "premium SaaS" unless the user asks for improvements.
- See `reference-ui-parity.mdc` for the full workflow and checklist.

The rules below apply when **no reference is provided**, or after reference parity is achieved.

When no reference exists, follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) for brand — not generic Linear/Vercel defaults. Shared component catalog: [docs/CODE_CONVENTIONS.md](../../docs/CODE_CONVENTIONS.md).

---

Every screen must feel:
- Spacious
- Intelligent
- Fast
- Interactive
- Premium

Every module must include:
- Empty states
- Skeleton loaders
- Error states
- Search states
- Success feedback
- Smooth transitions

Dashboard Rules:
- Modular widgets
- Draggable layout on web
- Collapsible sections
- Smart analytics cards
- AI insights cards

Forms:
- Multi-step where possible
- Auto-save drafts
- Smart validation
- Inline validation
- Progressive disclosure

Lists:
- Virtualized rendering
- Sticky filters
- Advanced search
- Smart sorting
- Batch actions

Chat UI:
- Streaming feel
- Typing indicators
- Citations
- Markdown support
- Copy actions
- AI thinking states
